        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: extract reusable AI runtime package",
        "body": "Closes #99040\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's model protocol adapters and streaming registry were embedded in the main application, so other packages could not reuse the proven Anthropic, OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Google, Vertex, Mistral, and ChatGPT/Codex transports without taking on OpenClaw's application runtime.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis extracts the provider-neutral contracts into the publishable `@openclaw/llm-core` package and the reusable runtime plus lazy provider adapters into `@openclaw/ai`. OpenClaw now consumes `@openclaw/ai` as a normal workspace/npm dependency; its existing registry, stream, plugin SDK, model routing, and provider behavior remain behind compatibility facades.\n\nThe runtime now supports isolated registry instances while retaining the process-default registry for existing callers. Built-in provider registration is table-driven, reducing production TypeScript by 210 lines, and the release workflow packs, verifies, and publishes both dependencies before the root package.\n\n## User Impact\n\nExisting OpenClaw users should see no configuration, model selection, authentication, or streaming behavior change. The root package installs an exact released `@openclaw/ai` dependency automatically; library consumers can separately create isolated runtimes and opt into the eight built-in API adapters.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm build` — full package declarations, root bundle, CLI/bootstrap guards, runtime postbuild, plugin SDK export check, and Control UI build passed.\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` passed with `packages/ai/dist` temporarily absent, proving clean-checkout source resolution.\n- Focused runtime/provider/build verification passed across four Vitest lanes: 261 tests total.\n- Packed `@openclaw/llm-core@2026.6.11` and `@openclaw/ai@2026.6.11`, installed both tarballs into an external npm consumer, compiled a strict NodeNext TypeScript consumer, registered all eight built-in APIs, and verified a second runtime remained isolated.\n- Emitted root chunks retain explicit `@openclaw/ai` imports; provider implementation is not duplicated into the OpenClaw bundle.\n- `actionlint .github/workflows/openclaw-npm-release.yml`, `pnpm plugins:sync:check`, formatting, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Autoreview completed clean after fixing its clean-checkout path-resolution finding.\n- Broad `pnpm check:changed` could not submit because the local Crabbox binary is 0.15.0 and current Testbox requires 0.22.0; hosted PR CI remains the broad gate.\n",
